language_examples:
Python (quick sample):
from redwood import Client
client = Client()
resp = client.generate(prompt='hello', idempotency_key='user-123-op-456', retry_preset='balanced')
# Streaming resume (opt-in):
s = client.chat_stream(prompt='long', enable_resume=True)
# on disconnect: s.resume(resume_token, idempotency_key='user-123-op-456')

TypeScript (quick sample):
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference'
const client = new Redwood()
const resp = await client.generate({ prompt: 'hi', idempotencyKey: 'u-123-op-456', retryPreset: 'balanced' })
// streaming resume
const stream = client.chat.stream({ enableResume: true })
// stream.resume(resumeToken, 'u-123-op-456')

Go (quick sample):
cli := redwood.NewClient(nil)
resp, _ := cli.Generate(context.Background(), redwood.GenerateParams{Prompt: "hi", IdempotencyKey: "u-123-op-456", RetryPreset: "balanced"})
// streaming resume pattern: client.StreamResume(ctx, resumeToken, idempotencyKey)
